essbook><name>NISHIKAWA, ARIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHKUBO, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UENO, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASAKI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAZAKI, FUMIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An easy process for producing a polyoxyalkylene polyol in which a residual catalyst compound is efficiently removed from a crude polyoxyalkylene polyol. The process is characterized by causing an active hydrogen compound to add an epoxide compound through addition polymerization with the aid of a compound having a P=N bond as a catalyst to produce a crude polyoxyalkylene polyol and contacting the crude polyoxyalkylene polyol with a solid acid having a specific surface area of 450 to 1,200 m&lt;2&gt;/g and an average pore diameter of 40 to 100  ANGSTROM  to regulate the amount of the catalyst remaining in the polyol to 150 ppm or smaller.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Procédé simple de production d'un polyol de polyoxyalkylène dans lequel un composé catalyseur résiduel est extrait efficacement d'un polyol de polyoxyalkylène brut. Le procédé est caractérisé par le fait qu'un composé d'hydrogène actif entraîne l'addition d'un composé epoxyde par la polymérisation par addition à l'aide d'un composé ayant une liaison P=N en tant que catalyseur, pour produire un polyol de polyoxyalkylène brut, et la mise en contact du polyol de polyoxyalkylène avec un acide solide ayant une surface spécifique de 450 à 1200 m&lt;2&gt;/g, et un diamètre de pore moyen de 40 à 100  ANGSTROM  afin de réguler la quantité du catalyseur restant dans le polyol à 150 ppm ou moins.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>